  "limits": [
    "Internal proofs are request-local typed authentication evidence, not externally accepted bearer tokens or a new persisted single-use token system. Stale proofs stay denied; external SIWE/reset replay protection remains nonce/token consumption in D1.",
    "No new durable credential counter or schema migration; exact salted hash serves as revision, including same-plaintext resets because salt changes.",
    "Authentication metadata/audit can record a successful credential check before a later mint denial; this change fences session authority, not transactional login telemetry across awaits.",
